@startuml sourcing-workflow

' ============================================================
' VISUAL THEME
' ============================================================
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam ArrowColor #57606A
skinparam DefaultFontName "SansSerif"
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF

skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  ParticipantBorderColor #57606A
  LifeLineBorderColor #57606A
  GroupBackgroundColor #F6F8FA
  GroupBorderColor #57606A
}
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF8C5
skinparam noteBorderColor #57606A

title ITIP Definition Blackboard Repository Sourcer - Sourcing workflow (single-Blackboard Run; in-memory SourcerContext + 3-panel confidence-weighted blackboard)

' ---- Client side (single JVM) ----
participant "ITIP Sourcer\n(RunDriver + RepoBootstrap)" as RD
participant "Producer KSs\n(RepoScan, ScipJava, Joern,\n Syft, SpringScan, JpaScan,\n TerraformParse, CodeGraphAssembly)" as Prod
participant "SourcerContext\n(in-memory only;\n NEVER persisted)" as Ctx
participant "Consumer KSs\n(*IdentificationKs,\n *ArchetypingKs,\n *StatementKs)" as Cons
participant "External tools\n(scip-java, joern-parse,\n syft, terraform parse)" as ExtT
participant "Inference service\n(LLM)" as Inf
participant "Client Reducer\n(controller-side)" as Red
participant "Post-reduction pipeline\n(validate + register to DefMan)" as PIPE

' ---- Substrate side ----
participant "REST API" as API
participant "Blackboard\nManager" as BBMgr
participant "Panel Registry" as PanelReg
participant "Contribution\nValidator" as Val
participant "Seal Manager" as Seal
database    "Blackboard\nStore + Audit" as Store

note over RD, Store
  **Scope** -- one client Run = one Blackboard.

  Radical re-design invariant: the blackboard hosts ONLY
  confidence-bearing identifications (`confidence.score < 1.0`).
  Deterministic tool outputs flow in-memory through `SourcerContext`
  between co-located producer and consumer KSs in a single JVM and
  are NEVER persisted (not on the blackboard, not on disk, not in
  any cache). Re-derivable on demand from `provenance.indexedRevision`
  + `provenance.tools[]`.

  Blackboard topology (3 panels; declared once, frozen on first POST):
   * `itip:Definition`  -- 6 *Identity slots
   * `itip:Archetype`   -- 6 *Archetype slots
   * `itip:Statement`   -- 6 *Statement slots
  Subjects (x6 per panel): Structure, Mechanism, DataArchetype,
  Effector, Receptor, Interaction.
end note

== Blackboard creation ==

RD -> RD : mint runId (client-side)
RD -> API : POST /blackboards\n  BlackboardConfig { name: "<repoLabel>",\n    auth: { writerSubjects: [...], bbAdminSubjects: [...] } }
API -> BBMgr : create Blackboard
BBMgr -> Store : persist Blackboard\n(status=OPEN, timestamp)
BBMgr --> API : 201 + bbId + ETag
API --> RD : 201 bbId, ETag

RD -> RD : RepoBootstrap.clone(gitUrl, ref)\n  -> working copy in JVM-local tempdir
RD -> RD : derive scope (include/exclude globs)\n  + profile

== Declare topology (3 panels x 6 slots = 18) ==

RD -> API : POST /blackboards/{bbId}/panels\n  PanelDeclaration[3]:\n    itip:Definition  (slots: {Structure,Mechanism,DataArchetype,Effector,Receptor,Interaction}Identity)\n    itip:Archetype   (slots: {Structure,Mechanism,DataArchetype,Effector,Receptor,Interaction}Archetype)\n    itip:Statement   (slots: {Structure,Mechanism,DataArchetype,Effector,Receptor,Interaction}Statement)\n  If-Match: <ETag>
API -> PanelReg : register panels + slots
PanelReg -> PanelReg : validate client-namespacing\n  + per-slot schemaUri form\n  + envelope $ref resolvability
PanelReg -> Store : persist panels + slots
PanelReg --> API : 201 + panelIds + ETag
API --> RD : 200 (DAG validated, schema URIs cached), new ETag

note right of PanelReg
  Topology is frozen on first contribution
  POST. Subsequent .../panels POSTs return 409.
end note

== Phase 1 - In-memory SourcerContext build (NO blackboard writes) ==

RD -> Prod : run Producer KSs (in dependency order)

Prod -> ExtT : execve scip-java (sandboxed)
ExtT --> Prod : .scip protobuf bytes
Prod -> Ctx : populate ScipIndex (parsed in JVM heap)

Prod -> ExtT : execve joern-parse / joern-export
ExtT --> Prod : CPG outputs
Prod -> Ctx : populate LoadedCpg

Prod -> ExtT : execve syft
ExtT --> Prod : SBOM (CycloneDX/SPDX)
Prod -> Ctx : populate Sbom

Prod -> Prod : in-process scan (Spring annotations,\n  JPA entities, Terraform HCL parse, ...)
Prod -> Ctx : populate FrameworkInventory + IacInventory

Prod -> Ctx : assemble CodeGraph\n  (joins ScipIndex + LoadedCpg + FrameworkInventory + IacInventory)

note right of Ctx
  At this point `SourcerContext` is fully built
  in JVM heap. Every Producer KS run is logged
  with its tool versions and outputs' digests
  for downstream `provenance.tools[]` capture.
  Nothing has touched the blackboard yet.
end note

== Phase 2 - Identification (write Definition panel) ==

loop for each Subject in {Structure, Mechanism, DataArchetype, Effector, Receptor, Interaction}

  RD -> Cons : run <Subject>IdentificationKs
  Cons -> Ctx : in-memory read (deterministic graphs)
  Cons -> Cons : embed non-deterministic selection\n  (e.g. Leiden inside StructureIdentificationKs;\n   taint-reach inside Effector/Receptor/Interaction;\n   structural heuristics inside DataArchetype/Mechanism)
  Cons -> API : POST /blackboards/{bbId}/contributions\n  (panel=itip:Definition, slot=<Subject>Identity,\n   post={subject, evidence[],\n         confidence:{score<1.0, method, factors[]},\n         provenance:{ks@version, indexedRevision,\n                     tools[], ruleSnapshotSha256, seeds[]}})

end

== Phase 3 - Archetyping (write Archetype panel) ==

loop for each Subject

  RD -> Cons : run <Subject>ArchetypingKs
  Cons -> API : GET /blackboards/{bbId}/state\n  (read upstream <Subject>Identity slot)
  Cons -> Ctx : in-memory read (refine match)
  Cons -> API : POST /blackboards/{bbId}/contributions\n  (panel=itip:Archetype, slot=<Subject>Archetype,\n   post={subject, evidence[], confidence, provenance})

end

== Phase 4 - Statement shaping (write Statement panel) ==

loop for each Subject

  RD -> Cons : run <Subject>StatementKs
  Cons -> API : GET /blackboards/{bbId}/state\n  (read upstream <Subject>Archetype slot)
  alt LLM-driven
    Cons -> Inf : completeStatement(archetypeMatch, evidence)
    Inf --> Cons : draft (carry inference cacheKey)
  else deterministic
    Cons -> Ctx : structural extraction
  end
  Cons -> API : POST /blackboards/{bbId}/contributions\n  (panel=itip:Statement, slot=<Subject>Statement,\n   post={subject, draftStatement, evidence[],\n         confidence, provenance})

end

note over API, Store
  Substrate-side handling of every contribution POST above:
    API -> Val : validate(post vs slot.schemaUri,
                          required confidence + provenance,
                          score < 1.0,
                          status=OPEN)
    alt accepted
      Val -> Store : append contribution (timestamp)
                  + audit-ledger entry (POSTED)
      Val --> API : 201 + contributionId
    else schema fail (e.g. score == 1.0 forbidden)
      Val --> API : 422 + diagnostics (NOT persisted)
    else blackboard not OPEN
      Val --> API : 409
    end
end note

== Seal (client asserts done) ==

RD -> API : POST /blackboards/{bbId}/seal\n  Authorization: Bearer <bb:seal scope>\n  If-Match: <ETag>
API -> Seal : transition Blackboard -> SEALING
Seal -> Store : reject further writes (409)
Seal -> Store : freeze contribution stream\n(byte-stable order:\npanel, slot, timestamp, id)
Seal -> Store : audit: seal event
Seal -> Store : Blackboard -> SEALED (sealTimestamp)
Seal --> API : 200 + sealTimestamp
API --> RD : 200 (status=SEALED)

== Read sealed contribution stream + reduce + register ==

RD -> API : GET /blackboards/{bbId}/contributions\n  ?panel=&slot=  (paginated; byte-stable)
API -> Store : load sealed stream slice
API --> RD : Contribution[]
RD -> Red : reduce per (panel, slot, subject)\n  using per-slot client policy (typically\n  highestConfidence over the *Statement slots);\n  log (reducerId, version, params,\n       inputContributionURIs[], outputValue)
Red --> RD : reducedView
RD -> PIPE : validate(reducedView) + register(Ascriptions)\n  to Definition Manager

note over PIPE
  Client-side. The substrate has no knowledge of "Ascription",
  "Definition Manager", or any GSM construct beyond opaque slot
  values. Reduction is itself a client-controller process; the
  substrate provides only the byte-stable sealed contribution
  stream as the replay anchor.

  Replayability: any contribution can be regenerated by re-running
  the named KS at the same `provenance.indexedRevision` with the
  same `provenance.tools[]` versions (rebuilds SourcerContext) and
  the same `provenance.ruleSnapshotSha256` + `provenance.seeds[]`
  (drives the embedded non-deterministic selection).
end note

== Blackboard isolation (no chaining) ==

note over RD, API
  Each Blackboard is fully isolated on the substrate side.
  `Contribution.derivedContribution[]` MUST reference contributions
  in the SAME Blackboard (cross-Bb URIs are rejected with 422).
  Cross-Bb lineage (if any) lives in the client's own log.
end note

== Licensing attention point (design-time, MUST resolve before commercial ship) ==

note over Prod, ExtT #FFD7D5
  **External-tool licensing audit -- BLOCKING for commercial Poesis distribution.**

  If `StructureIdentificationKs` embeds `leidenalg` (Python, GPL-3.0)
  in-process, copyleft may extend to the host JVM via the embedded
  Python sandbox. Mitigations (pick one before ship):
   (a) replace with `python-louvain` (BSD) or `cdlib` (BSD-3);
   (b) isolate `leidenalg` behind a separate sandboxed subprocess
       so the host process is not "combined work";
   (c) accept GPL-3.0 obligations for the distributed binary.

  Default safe path: (a) -- swap to `python-louvain`. Slightly lower
  modularity quality; entire stack stays under permissive licenses.
end note

@enduml
